    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0935" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861b.6363/86</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Sinclair Exploration Company</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Department is in receipt of your
                    letter of October 24, 1923, stating that your company has recently despatched a
                    party to the Far East with instructions to proceed to the “Russian half of the
                    Island of Sakhalin, and there commence exploratory work for oil.” You add that
                    “this work is undertaken in fulfillment of the concessional contract, for the
                    exploration and development of the oil resources of Sakhalin, originally entered
                    into between the <pb facs="0936" n="812" xml:id="pg812"/> Sinclair Exploration
                    Company and the Far Eastern Republic, and since ratified in August of this year
                    by the Moscow Government.”</p>
                <p>In acknowledging the receipt of your letter this Department refers you to its
                    letter of March 17, 1923.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Under
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
